      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ffa703c1-807e-5ce2-84ba-1c6432e92bca",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Junkers Flugzeug- und Motorenwerke AG (Junkers)\n- Products: Pirna 014 axial turbojet\n- People: Former Junkers engineers\n- Places: East Germany, Soviet Union, Dessau\n\nFacts:\n- Junkers Flugzeug- und Motorenwerke AG was a major German aircraft and aircraft engine manufacturer based in Dessau, Germany.\n- Junkers produced some of the world's most innovative and best-known airplanes during its more than fifty-year history in Dessau, Germany.\n- After World War II, former Junkers engineers were held in custody in the Soviet Union and were repatriated to East Germany in 1954.\n- In the mid- to late 1950s, those former Junkers engineers designed the Pirna 014, an axial turbojet, in East Germany.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
